{
  "_comment": "The setup screen's rules, shared by both plugins. `delivery`: a cron job's delivery target as a channel binding pattern (Hermes `deliver: \"<platform>:<to>\"`, OpenClaw an announce delivery with that channel and to), null for a person, a phone number, a thread or anything not a room. `covers`: whether a grant in force (existing) already covers an item (candidate): the same kind, the same pattern (case ignored except for files) or `*.` over the domain and every name under it, or a file folder's `/*` over a file directly in it, and allows no narrower. `warnings`: the warnings an item carries from its own kind, pattern and allows. `registrable`: the registrable domain of a host, in ASCII. `describe`: the item's first line, in the plugin's words (lifetime in minutes, null for until revoked or removed). `last`: how long ago the last approved review was, by UTC calendar day. `exposure`: whether a scan response flags exposure (an `exposure.*` reason, or exposure or session_exposure above 0). `notes`: the agent's reason as the screen shows it, inside a code span so links, mentions and emphasis do nothing (null: no note line).",
